Article 8
(1) Regional Government in efforts to protect children is responsible for:
a. Guaranteeing the existence of children without discrimination in accordance with statutory regulations;
b. Providing support for facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of child protection;
c. Guaranteeing the right of children to express opinions in accordance with the age and intelligence level of the child;
d. Establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for the protection of children's rights;
e. Conducting cooperation with the community and/or community organizations in the implementation of child protection in accordance with statutory regulations;
f. Conducting rehabilitation for children who are victims of acts of violence;
g. Providing special protection to children in emergency situations, children in conflict with the law, children who are victims of acts of violence and human trafficking, children from minority and isolated groups, children exploited economically and/or sexually, children who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic substance abuse and children with HIV/AIDS;
h. Organizing inclusive education for children with special needs, and
i. Taking preventive actions in order to prevent violations of children's rights.
(2) The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to protect children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by SKPD in accordance with its duties and functions.

Part One
Regional Government Article 7 (1) The Regional Government in efforts to protect women is responsible for:
a. Guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with laws and regulations;
b. Establishing and implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women's rights;
c. Conducting cooperation with the community and/or community organizations in the implementation of women's protection in accordance with laws and regulations;
d. Conducting rehabilitation and empowerment of women who are victims of violence;
e. Providing special protection to women victims of violence and human trafficking, and
f. Taking preventive actions in order to prevent violations of women's rights.
(2) The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to protect women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by SKPD in accordance with their duties and functions.

Article 13
(1) In order to prevent violations of women's rights, the Regional Government:
a. Conducts Socialization regarding the prevention of violence against women by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. Provides guidelines on handling acts of violence against women;
c. Involves community participation in recovery and social reintegration;
d. Develops an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against women;
e. Develops family empowerment programs;
f. Strengthens the function of community organizations working in the field of women's empowerment; and
g. Provides public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women.
(2) In order to prevent violations of children's rights, the Regional Government:
a. Undertakes efforts to prevent acts of violence against children by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. Develops child-friendly schools;
c. Encourages increased participation of children through the establishment of children's forums;
d. Provides guidelines on handling acts of violence against children;
e. Involves community participation in recovery services and reintegration of child victims of violence.
f. Develops an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against children;
g. Strengthens the function of community organizations working in the field of child protection; and
h. Realizes the development of a Child-Friendly City; Realizes Child-Friendly Open Public Spaces (RPTRA).

